{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "ad47925b-7258-4442-a9af-412c7f76d753",
    "name": "Cohabit API",
    "description": "API collection for the Cohabit platform.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Import this collection and the `cohabit-api.postman_environment.json` environment.\n2. Select the **Cohabit API (local)** environment in the top-right dropdown.\n3. `baseUrl` defaults to `http://localhost:5001` (cohabit API) and `commsBaseUrl` to `http://localhost:5002` (comms API, both Aspire-hosted).\n4. The OTP endpoints require a Bearer token: paste a JWT (with `sub`, `phone_number` and `email` claims) into the `token` environment variable.\n\n**Seeded data**\nLookup ids (provinces, listing types, amenities, rules, verification types) and entity ids (user, address, listing) are pre-loaded as environment variables, so you don't need to call list endpoints first. After a successful create request, the id is auto-captured into the environment for follow-up update/delete requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Provinces",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List all provinces",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
